# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for tonight's four-card window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/serve-3 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN.
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. Every value is final.
# ORDER.txt says the order, each job's image, its stop rule and its minutes. The image is tp4-serve-3 throughout: T1 builds it, the
# later jobs serve it, and a commit after T1's tag needs a new tag and every later job the new one.
# T4 (optional): the formal exactness of the tail caps on long real-text prompts, the S3a matrix (X2's passing shape): four
# concurrent users against each solo, so the 4->3->2->1 budget tails are served by capped packed rounds. The traffic profile
# c2-packed-tp4 on the new image. C2_GATE_PLAN may become 'matrix,staggered' if 60 more minutes are free.
# Pass: gate exit 0 under the strict policy (every concurrent text equals its solo text), 0 audit mismatches, and packed budget-cap
# lines in the concurrent arm. Run it only if T1 passed and tp4-serve-3 is wanted in service soon; otherwise it goes to the next
# window with the four-card platform replay of a tp4-serve-3 thin layer.
# Duration (estimate): 75 min.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset gate
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-3
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4
C2_GATE_PLAN=matrix
C2_GATE_LENGTHS=4096,16384,32768,60000
C2_GATE_MAX_TOKENS=512
C2_GATE_JIT=record
